reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:91:## L14 — Paddle overwrites the core-computed next payment date, without rescheduling
reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:93:`PaddleGateway.php:1379-1384` calls `markOrderPaid()` (which triggers the whole core fan-out including `_next_payment_date` recomputation and `RenewalScheduler::schedule()`) and **then** `syncNextPaymentDate()` (`:2289-2306`) rewrites `_next_payment_date` from Paddle's `next_billed_at` **without touching Action Scheduler**. The queued legs can therefore point at a different moment than the stored date until the next hourly sweep. Never assert AS-timestamp/meta agreement on a Paddle subscription.
reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:95:## L15 — Paddle writes `_last_payment_failure` as a Unix timestamp
reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:97:`PaddleGateway.php:1435`: `update_post_meta($subscription_id, '_last_payment_failure', time());` — everywhere else this meta is a UTC MySQL string (`RenewalProcessor.php:580`, `handleFailure()` `:733`). Anything that renders or compares this value (admin timeline, `can_retry_payment` gating) will see `1785000000` instead of a date on Paddle failures. **Genuine bug candidate.**
reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:101:`RenewalProcessor::process()` treats `requires_action` as a success-ish state (`:404-406` → `handleManualPaymentPending()` `:552-567`, returns `true`). No `failed` order status, no `payment_failed` email, no retry, `_payment_retry_attempts` stays 0 — but the grace clock still cancels the subscription at ≈ D+4 days. Expect exactly one email (`renewal_requires_verification`) for the whole SCA sequence.
reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:109:`arraysubs/src/functions/gateway-helpers.php:202`: `interval_seconds = max(HOUR_IN_SECONDS, …)`. Any filter that tries to shorten retries for testing cannot go below 3600 s.
