reference/SLT-REF-10-known-landmines-fragile-order-dependent-and-time-travel-host.md:141:Some call sites parse dates as `strtotime($date)` (`RenewalProcessor::isRenewalDue()` `:538`, `ProrationCalculator::getDaysUsed()` `:444`), others as `strtotime($date . ' UTC')` (`Hooks.php:447,663`, `EarlyRenewManager.php:137`). These agree **only because WordPress forces `date_default_timezone_set('UTC')`**. Do not "fix" a test by relying on the bare form, and never change the PHP process timezone. Sync boundaries, by contrast, are computed in **site time (UTC+6)** and converted to UTC for storage (`renewal-sync-helpers.php:245,253,385-392`) — a monthly boundary of "1st 00:00 site" is stored as `…-<last day> 18:00:00` UTC. Expect that 6-hour shift in every stored synced date.
